      <Comment>|FRAME:Lysophospholipids &quot;A lysophospholipid&quot;| is a phospholipid in which one of the fatty acids is replaced with a hydroxyl group. When the backbone of the lipid is |FRAME: GLYCEROL| (|FRAME: Phosphoglycerides|), the hydroxyl group may be on carbon 1, in which case the compound is named |FRAME: 1-Lyso-phospholipids|, or on carbon 2, in which case it is named |FRAME: 2-Lyso-phospholipids|.</Comment>
